

- State pattern is a behavioural pattern that implements a state machine
in an object-oriented way.With that state pattern, each state is implemented as
a derived class of a state interface ,and state transitions are handled by involving methods
defined by interfaces.

- variant of strategy pattern

Example - Automatic Coffee machine
          Idle -> selecting -> dispensing

          interface -> concrete classes -> state class -> main class calling state class

when to use:

If an object behavior depends on its state and needs to change dynamically at runtime based on
state transitions, then consider.

--Automatic coffe machine, vending machines, order management

Summary:

The state design pattern separates state and behaviour , allowing objects to dynamically adjust
their behaviour based on their state.This pattern improves system flexibility and maintainability
enabling easy managment and extesnsion of an object statelogic